{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082960-what-would-the-world-look-like-if-the-sons-of-ether-had-dominated-the-technocracy","id":1082960,"title":"What would the world look like if the Sons of Ether had dominated the Technocracy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-24T04:13:18-07:00","id":1082960,"title":"What would the world look like if the Sons of Ether had dominated the Technocracy","content":"Let's say that the Sons of Ether had been far, far more politically successful within the Techocracy, becoming the dominate convention. The other conventions still exist, but even they become essentially specialized variations on the Etherite paradigm. How does both Mage and human history change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T04:15:20-07:00","id":1082961,"title":"","content":"A Flash Gordon reel combined with the worse excesses of steam punk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:24:24-07:00","id":1083002,"title":"","content":"Not great, but not in the way that most folks are going to comment, I'd wager.<br /> <br /> Consider Czar Vargo as a model of what the pre-split Etherites are like. He's well-meaning, adventurous, courageous, but also small-t-technocratic. When Vargo liberated the world, his ultimatum was not that the people would be free to choose their own way of life - it was that the governments of the world would surrender the reigns of power to <i>Vargo </i>and to &quot;scientific&quot; control. Vargo takes it for granted that those that possess the appropriate philosophical and educational qualifications will be able to &quot;solve&quot; governance, like it's a math problem. This strand of high modernism is part of the thematic underpinning of the Union, but it's clearly present in the early Etherites too - and the things that temper that thread are born of lessons learned when they were on the outside as a Tradition. Lessons they would not have to learn, if they were a dominant Convention. Look at 50s and 60s sci-fi. Not for the cackling mad scientists - there may be a few, but it's not important - but for the scene where the lantern-jawed white guy scientist is put in charge of a military formation, or negotiates with an alien race on Earth's behalf.<br /> <br /> Globally, lots of technocratic communism and isolationist &quot;Third Way&quot; fascism. Ether-based utopian technology empowers these societies to provide for their needs, but the Etherites in this time line never get an anti-authoritarian streak, so while they may disapprove of Etheric North Korea (a militarized dictatorship whose borders are sealed by impenetrable Etheric Shields), they don't have any Utopians agitating to <i>do </i>something about it. The statist Etherites smother the anarchist Difference Engineers in the crib. Without a push for a unified globe, there's no global internet, but a series of national &quot;telenetworks&quot;, which means no &quot;digital frontier&quot; for the Virtual Adepts.<br /> <br /> The technocratic influence means that every major government devotes a lot of funding to scientific research towards practical ends - super-crops, fuels, etc. - and that these &quot;science ministries&quot; have a lot of social and political clout, something akin to a state religion. The &quot;Etheric N.W.O&quot; convention is made up of and influences these &quot;scientific advisors&quot; instead of controlling faceless bureaucracies or top-secret intelligence agencies.<br /> <br /> Space stations and bases on the moon and mars. Space remains a nationalist and militarized endeavor, so the &quot;etheric void engineers&quot; are a secret conspiracy within various national space programs. They trade information and coordinate, but they don't share resources - there are Russian voidships with Russian crews, and American ships, and sometimes they work together to deal with an alien threat, but with gritted teeth. There's also less &quot;esprit de corps&quot; and a greater focus on the individual - modernism deified the astronaut as the soldier-scientist-explorer, so the &quot;ether marines&quot; are composed of a bunch of people that each see themselves as the hero of their own movie.<br /> <br /> ItX and the Progenitors don't change much, but they no longer have a Syndicate that determines which projects to fund or a global capitalist economy to internationalize R&amp;D and manufacturing, they're much more embedded into their surroundings - they have to make a case to their local amalgam why some Primal resources ought to be dedicated to their project, and that local amalgam is probably made up of people from the same country. So it's less &quot;why does the Union want to fund this&quot; and more &quot;why should we divert Primal resources from Russia to pay for your project, comrade?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Etherites don't have an ethics board until the 40s, and don't start to acknowledge the contributions of women and minorities until the 60s. This Union isn't mustache-twirling about it, but there's almost certainly a glass ceiling - the regional board that coordinates Union efforts in a given nation is upper-class, it's male. It's probably white, and where it isn't, it's made up of the dominant ethnic group. Ethical oversight is slapdash and ad hoc; nobody is Conditioned, and the sort of experiments that would get you executed in Nation A may be overlooked in Nation B.<br /> <br /> <b>tl;dr:</b> Instead of one Technocratic Union, you have the Technocratic Society of [America, Russia, etc.], and the Societies work together to ensure that Science and Reason guide the world, but don't have any globe-spanning agenda - each Society may resent or work against the others. No girls allowed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:41:53-07:00","id":1083010,"title":"","content":"There are a few elements of Technocratic Etherites that I think would rise to the forefront.<br /> <br /> 1) Most research would be driven by Individual scientists - The Etherites are remnants of a time when a lot of scientific research came from wealthy individuals rather than grand industrial cooperation. That's an element the Technocracy phased out after they left, to the point that Jobs and Wozniak starting a tech giant in their garage is the exception rather than the rule.<br /> <br /> 2) Scientific study would be more elegant - I think the idea of Science as a form of personal expression happened after the Etherites split from their former allies, but they've always preferred theories that are elegant and imaginative over those that are expedient. Indeed that was part of what led to their punishment. In an Etherite led Technocracy clinical and unemotional science would take a back seat to dramatic and compelling science.. <br /> <br /> 3) The Technocracy would be even more authoritarian than it is now - The SoE embodies a lot of classic science fiction idealism, which includes things like scientific idealism and fascist utopias. Having to rebel against the authority of the rest of the technocracy changed that for them, as did their time with the Traditions, and even then one of their most famous members tried to take over the entire world to impose his ideas of peace. I suspect that if they'd never had to confront the possibility of a flawed scientific hegemony they'd be much, much worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T08:34:29-07:00","id":1083026,"title":"","content":"If we believe in their book, one of the big things Sons of Ether wanted to disclose to the world, against the wishes of the Syndicate, was &quot;free energy&quot;, that added with the rejection of ether led to the formation of the Etherites. This two facts make for a case that an Union leaded by the Ether it's going to be less focused with a global agenda and more tolerant with individual Masters that want to push their agendas (but not necesarily with agents of the lower levels). The Technocracy it's going to be more elitist, and focused in big, bold, leaders and heros that will make the politic.<br /> Oh, and there may be &quot;free energy&quot; in some places of the world and there's no &quot;outer space devoid of life&quot; and more &quot;etherspace where people can breath&quot;.<br /> <br /> However, if the Sons of Ether have had one characteristic even before leaving the Union, it's their flamboyance. This would mean Paradox. We would have a Union much less scared of Paradox.<br /> <br /> The Traditions would have to fear bolder attacks of an enemy that doesn't care so much for the consequences (if this would play better for the Union or the Traditions it's to be seen).<br /> <br /> Technological advancement would be more unpredictable, more prone to failure, as the Etherites push to advance the Time Table a lot faster than the NWO. While this may deteriorate the trust in bleeding edge researches and stuff, it will also increase the technological advancement. Depending on how well this it's handled it may erode the exeptiscism in utopical science, or weaken the belief in science. Think on physic gabinets, scientists disclosing their (not the, but their) late milacre of science, sometimes it may not work, but those who do will generate a lot of prestigee for the genius behind the product.<br /> <br /> We would be exploring a space with aliens where people can breath! We will live in a hollow earth!. Of course, the might decide to not disclose all this data, to not scare people with the dangerous beings that live out there. However, I would say that, at least, they will try to disclose the existence of the less dangerous aliens, to prepare people for the inevitable colonization of the etherspace (that, again, they will try to push sooner than latter).<br /> <br /> Dependant on how people reacts to all of this and how Paradox reacts to all of this, we may live in a much more fantastical world, or not, but surely it would be more unpredictable than it already is. At the very least, I imagine a world where people worship geniuses. Science and corporations would be less of a stable development of the &quot;system&quot; and more the product of great people. It would be a more elitist society, in that regards, with (even) less patience for &quot;the incompetent and the lazy&quot;.<br /> Also, we may live in a world less interested in products or useful tools, and more in theory and knowledge. This may sound nice and dandy, but it also may mean that you wouldn't be able to buy a computer and expect it to be &quot;intuitive&quot; (that's for the lazy, wanna use MY new and original computer? learn the theory behind it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-24-2017, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:07:22-07:00","id":1083040,"title":"","content":"Something between William Gibson and Bruce Sterling's <i>The Difference Engine</i> and <i>Girl Genius</i>? <br /> <br /> I guess the big question is WHEN did this happen? I mean, the Sons of Ether were never part of the Technocracy, so was this changeover back in the days of the Voltarian Order? (I keep seeing a steampunk Queen Victoria... Hmmm that brings to mind to George Mann's Newberry and Hobbes and Ghost of... books). Or was it later, in the days of the Electrodyne Engineers?<br /> <br /> I disagree about the idea that the Analytical Reckoners/Virtual Adepts would have been folded in. If IBM/Iteration-X is going to stay separate, the whole thrust of &quot;individial achievement&quot; would probably have led to MORE Conventions rather than less. <br /> <br /> The Void Engineers would certainly be a different kettle of fish. There might not even be the whole concept of &quot;Etherites... I mean Electrodyne Engineers... in space.&quot; There's already a Convention for that. Hells, maybe there would still be something of s division between the gentleman explorers and space explorers, redividing the Void Engineers back up into two Conventions. <br /> <br /> The N.W.O probably didn't happen and the Ivory Tower still stands tall as a think-tank Convention for the creation of ideologies and less of the implementation of one true ideology to bring us all together and bind us. <br /> <br /> Differentiating IBM/It-X from the Voltarians/EE seems weird. It's like &quot;boring&quot; vs. &quot;exciting&quot;. And if &quot;exciting&quot; is SOP, then maybe the whole thing started with a struggle between the Voltarians/EEs and IBM/It-X and the Volatrians/EEs won... So there is no clockwork or assembly line Convention. That kind of science is what went the way of the Ether is this alternate world.<br /> <br /> In some ways, it's more like the whole point is to have the idea of SCIENCE! infect the Union as a whole, that means that it's probably going to be the other Conventions bending towards the various methods as described by other posters. It's not so much that the SoE influenced the Union as the whole Union becomes a set of Conventions that break out and more fully develop some of the SoE tropes.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of ways this can go, but a lot of it depends on the starting parameters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:50:05-07:00","id":1083120,"title":"","content":"and then they discover Cthulhu. Because SOMEBODY had to take that Mystic Science merit. And that's Cthulhu. Enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:48:45-07:00","id":1083168,"title":"","content":"Assuming a greater focus on individual scientists and scientific pursuit and a greater focus on utopian ideals and authoritarianism, this is what I see happening to the other Conventions.<br /> <br /> Iteration X is greatly changed. There was always a lot of overlap between them, the Electrodyne Engineers, and the Difference Engineers. That was fine when the other two were minor Conventions, but with the Etherites in ascendancy they don't have much of a place. They are still one half of the Military Industrial Complex, but with less ability to predict the next revolutionary leap that Complex is diminished. I see them becoming an applied science division. Someone needs to translate the diverse products of the rest of the Technocracy into reliable and trustworthy devices. They might keep being the robotic faction, though.<br /> <br /> The Progenitors are hit in a similar way, but they weather it better. Partly because making things for sleepers is what they already do and partly because the need for medicine and other treatments is a constant. Their techniques might be different but their focus is largely the same. On the other hand, the Progenitors have always straddled the ethics issue, being both the conscience of the Technocracy and the Convention most tempted to cross the line. The ideals of the Etherites are going to put that struggle into stark relief.<br /> <br /> The Void Engineers will thrive under the Etherites (or be subsumed into them). The independent scientist and the independent explorer are two sides of the same coin so they were natural bedfellows. The VEs will still have much of the same focus they already do. Although perhaps they will have a greater emphasis on sanitizing the new frontiers rather than defining them.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate, as the other half of the Military Industrial Complex don't enjoy quite the same power. They're the ones that have to tell everyone else no, and that is harder to do in an Etherite world. Not to mention that the Etherite dream of free power, while it fits into Syndicate ideals in the long term, severely cuts into their ability to manipulate society in the short term.<br /> <br /> The NWO though, they're doing really well. Someone needs to be there to turn those utopian ideals into a coherent and stable government and the NWO more than willing to do the job. While they do lose quite a bit of direct control, they end us as all but equal partners with the Etherites.<br /> <br /> The Difference Engineers will rise and fall and rebel. Computers are a cool new technology but their utility is deeply tied to the vast infrastructure the classic Technocracy pushed forward. There will eventually be an internet, but its probably going to come more slowly, and computers may be a very different thing by that point. More than any other faction they need reliability and predictability and they will be rebuffed when they ask for it. So, the way I see it, while everyone else is focused on what can be done, the Difference Engineers and ItX will be threading applied technology with standard practices that eveyone can understand. When the time is right and their protocols are too deeply entrenched to uproot, a big chunk of them will jump ship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T18:02:30-07:00","id":1083245,"title":"","content":"One of the key things to remember with an &quot;ascendant Son of Ether&quot; ideology is that a lot of what Sons of Ether do in the Traditions, they now WON'T be doing.<br /> <br /> No kooky biological experiments. The Progenitors will be doing those.<br /> No more intrepid Etherite adventurers. That's what the Void Engineers are for.<br /> Etc.<br /> After all this is the Technocratic <i>Union</i>, which is based on diversification of portfolios and interdependence. <br /> <br /> The one that will probably stay true to form will be the Syndicate. (I would throw the N.W.O in, but, without the defection of the Etherites, Czar Vargo, et al. there won't BE a N.W.O.)<br /> <br /> Sure, they will be doing those things in ways reminiscent of what became the Etherites in that other, less interesting, world, but the Electrodyne Engineers won't be replacing those other groups, more infecting them with a specific ideological bent.<br /> <br /> I really don't what IBM/Iteration-X is going to be doing, since, effectively, they are defined by being NOT like that. In fact, it does make sense that, if the Electrodyne Engineers win instead of the work-a-day drudge science of IBM, it might IBM/It-X that gets the heave ho. If they are still around, it's probably going to be somehow allied with the Syndicate or some rather grim ideologies cooked up in the Ivory Tower as a sort of &quot;dehumanized, assembly-line&quot; Convention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T04:39:43-07:00","id":1083406,"title":"","content":"I figure any exile or rebellion should have a reason or event associated with it. The Etherites and the VAs left over differences in vision but there were also triggering events like the disproving of the luminiferous ether and the persecution of Turing.<br /> <br /> If I had to choose such a scenario for ItX, it would be the revelation of The Computer as a spirit. The embarrassment from that would destroy their influence in the Technocracy for generations and could be the foundation of all sorts of bad blood. It could also kick off a few new lines of scientific inquiry the Ex-Iterators could take with them if they joined the other side.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T11:54:03-07:00","id":1084610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082960-what-would-the-world-look-like-if-the-sons-of-ether-had-dominated-the-technocracy?p=1083406#post1083406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure any exile or rebellion should have a reason or event associated with it. The Etherites and the VAs left over differences in vision but there were also triggering events like the disproving of the luminiferous ether and the persecution of Turing.<br /> <br /> If I had to choose such a scenario for ItX, it would be the revelation of The Computer as a spirit. The embarrassment from that would destroy their influence in the Technocracy for generations and could be the foundation of all sorts of bad blood. It could also kick off a few new lines of scientific inquiry the Ex-Iterators could take with them if they joined the other side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a solid date on when that happened? I mean the name change to Iteration-X, not the revelation the Computer was a spirit. Which seems like a way to nerf the Convention in a crap way. (What other group is so UTTERLY compromised as that? So fundamentally duped? It makes the Ksifrai = House Janissary thing seem like a low-grade market rebranding exercise. And I can't think of anything even as bad as that for any other Sect. Well... except for the Technocracy being, at its core, the Technephandi and always having been such...) <br /> <br /> I look at the material and it seems like it's put at different times in different location. And when IBM became Iteration-X would probably be the key to telling this alternate story. It makes no sense really. Why are they even building a computer? Aren't the Virtual Adepts (or whatever they called at that exact moment) the computer people? So why is IBM building the biggest baddest computer? Seems like it should be the Techno-VA's who should have jumped on that and THEY'D be the ones to change their name to Iteration-X.<br /> <br /> Instead of IBM as the face of a conspiracy selling the &quot;No luminerous ether&quot; idea at the Symposium and getting it taken up for the latest (dare I say it?) iteration of the Time Table, maybe the Electrodyne Engineers revealed that IBM was poaching from the VA's and building a self-aware machine. Though that would mean the idea of creating artificial (or perhaps artificial mechanical) life was anathema for some reason.... Not sure why that would be. Maybe that's what the Electrodyne Engineers are able to sell as the &quot;Great Sin&quot; and get them kicked out or gacked like the Craftmasons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T12:59:22-07:00","id":1084649,"title":"","content":"I ran into similar problems. It doesn't seem like the Iterators should have changed their name until after the VAs left, but they did. I suppose it could have happened while the ARs were in their infancy, but then why didn't the Computer go with them. It's odd.<br /> <br /> I think the moment of their name change is the best moment for their fall and the Etherites rise. They put a lot of energy into defining themselves and it ended up backfiring in a major way. If that's the case their humiliation must have something to do with the Computer, computers, or AI in general. Also, in normal Technocracy history it didn't matter if ItX poached from the Difference Engineers. If it did the name change would have been all the proof anyone needed. Given that, I see two major possibilities.<br /> <br /> 1) The Computer is unveiled and revealed at the same event. It's not quite as politically damaging a revelation as it would be a generation later, and only the project leaders really face censure. However the name Iteration X becomes a running joke among the other Conventions, and it follows them through their hasty re-branding. They aren't in any place to disprove the Ether, and industrial engineering is set back 20 years.<br /> <br /> 2) Perhaps there was a Technocracy wide push to get an AI or Autonomous Servant on the timetable and IBM and the Etherites were racing to fill that spot. Because it was a contest to show who was more capable, the revelation that ItX had poached was much more damning than it would normally have been. Computer AI won but ItX lost major credibility (or, if you want an even stranger world the Etherite's proposition won and ItX and the DEs were both shamed).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T18:04:31-07:00","id":1084790,"title":"","content":"I think it would be REALLY humiliating to have your Convention develop a secret goal which required poaching pretty much completely from another Convention, jiggering that stuff for whatever you thought your actual reason was for doing this whole thing, then having it found out that, not only did you not accomplish what you wanted, but that you did exactly the opposite of the entire intent of the creation of the Order of Reason back in the first place.<br /> <br /> Especially if it was revealed at the big unveiling of the new name by a punch of punk pulp adventurer types. <br /> <br /> The core question would be what that reason was. If it was &quot;get an AI&quot;... it seems like that was already something that they or the VAs/Difference Engineers could do already. Progenitors were making intelligent artificial as it is. It doesn't seem impossible that there would be some steam powered clockwork talking head thing out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T20:14:44-07:00","id":1084832,"title":"","content":"If you wanted to do something wacky with the Iterators:<br /> <br /> In the 30s when Autochthonia is rediscovered, the lion's share of the Artificers (whateverthehell they're called at the time) and Reckoners migrate there - there is less pressing need to monitor earthside events with the Union unbroken, and the returned Construct is the discovery of a lifetime, after all, the product of over a century of unimpeded Enlightened Artifice. Instead of the Computer being some alien spirit, it's a joint construct of the minds of the 18th century Artificers that were stranded on Auto and the &quot;chorus&quot; of Iterators and Reckoners that join with it. The Autochthonian Collective Intelligence is a pseudo-Convention composed of artificial intelligences and Artificers that have willingly undergone Disconnection to live full-time as part of Autochthon. In effect, the ACI is acybernetic transhuman species that maintains friendly relationships with the Union, but focuses the majority of its attentions on self-improvement and exploration of the outer reaches of the Tellurian (and the depths of the Digital Web.)<br /> <br /> This lets you use &quot;it was invented by our 'alien allies'&quot; as an origin for your wild sci-fi ray weapons, and it gets the Convention <i>mostly </i>out of the picture without them really defecting or being wiped out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T05:43:52-07:00","id":1084981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082960-what-would-the-world-look-like-if-the-sons-of-ether-had-dominated-the-technocracy?p=1084790#post1084790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be REALLY humiliating to have your Convention develop a secret goal which required poaching pretty much completely from another Convention, jiggering that stuff for whatever you thought your actual reason was for doing this whole thing, then having it found out that, not only did you not accomplish what you wanted, but that you did exactly the opposite of the entire intent of the creation of the Order of Reason back in the first place.<br /> <br /> Especially if it was revealed at the big unveiling of the new name by a punch of punk pulp adventurer types.<br /> <br /> The core question would be what that reason was. If it was &quot;get an AI&quot;... it seems like that was already something that they or the VAs/Difference Engineers could do already. Progenitors were making intelligent artificial as it is. It doesn't seem impossible that there would be some steam powered clockwork talking head thing out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, AI seems too banal. Perhaps the goal was a construct with the capacity for Enlightened Science. It's a much harder goal and one the Etherites might even have the advantage on. R&amp;D for it could plausibly involve experiments on extradimensional entities.<br /> <br /> I could see the Iterators seeing a promising DE experiment, stealing it, running it through their iterative programming and unveiling it only for it to be shot down. Then when they tried to pin the blame on the DEs it would turn out the original experiment was actually about creating an artificial extradimensional entity.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T13:29:51-07:00","id":1089925,"title":"","content":"If you've never seen it, try to find a copy of GURPS Alternate Earths (vol. 1) from Steve Jackson Games. One of the six worlds detailed is called Gernsback, and is a world in which Nikola Tesla married Anne Morgan (daughter of J.P. Morgan), ultimately resulting in a world full of 1930s science fiction technology.<br /> <br /> (The other five worlds are the Nazi's winning WW2, the Confederacy winning the American Civil War, two dominated by the Romans and the Aztecs, respectively, and a deeply weird one that mixes cyberpunk with a world run by a Christianized Japan, a Soviet style Swedish empire, the Empire of Brazil and a surviving French monarchy.)<br /> <br /> ((Vol 2 has world dominated by the Imperial Chinese and a global Caliphate, if you've ever wondered what a world dominated by the Wu Lung or Ahl i Batin might look like.))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 05-08-2017, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}